  "note": "Independent re-judgment after export-chain next-hop unification (cabc8c511e / c2d7117d05) against RFC 2545 Section 3: 'A BGP speaker shall advertise to its peer in the Network Address of Next Hop field the global IPv6 address of the next hop, potentially followed by the link-local IPv6 address of the next hop.' Re-read all changed test files and production producers (forward_next_hop.go, peer_forward_facts.go, egress_inject_filter.go). In next_hop_family_admission_test.go::TestFamilyNextHopForwardAdmission, only the later-repair subcase moved from NextHopExplicit to [edit, next-hop:self] via exportNextHopPolicy (exercising applyRawOverrideNextHopIntent with afterRaw=true) while preserving all 5 families, both rails, and exact MP_REACH/MP_UNREACH byte assertions. In rfc2545_forward_subnet_test.go and rfc4659_link_local_peering_test.go, NextHopMode=NextHopUnchanged moved to setExportNextHopUnchanged and repairWith moved to [raw-next-hop, next-hop:self] with identical global-first, link-local-second, unusable-global refusal, and legacy-sibling assertions. In test/plugin/adj-rib-in-replay-rfc2545-next-hop.ci, config migrated to bus + export { filters [ next-hop:unchanged ]; final accept; } + rs-client true; both seq=1 live control and seq=2 adj-rib-in replay still assert exact wire hex carrying 0x20 + 2001:db8::1 + fe80::1 (only AS_PATH shortened to [65001] for transparent rs-client). All other 31 tagged tests are unchanged. Q1-Q4 satisfied; polarity pairs intact. Source-level judgment only.",
